        "Sit on the left foot laid flat, keep the right foot upright with its toes towards the Qibla, and rest the hands on the thighs near the knees." to "Keti kwa mguu wa kushoto uliowekwa sawa, uweke mguu wa kulia ulio sawa na vidole vyake kuelekea Qibla, na uweke mikono juu ya mapaja karibu na magoti.",
        "Sit on the left hip with both feet out to the right side, and rest the hands on the thighs with the fingers together." to "Kaa kwenye kiuno cha kushoto na miguu yote miwili nje upande wa kulia, na uweke mikono kwenye mapaja na vidole pamoja.",
        "At ‘ash-hadu al-la ilaha’ raise the index finger of the right hand, and lower it at ‘illallah’." to "Katika ‘ash-hadu al-la ilaha’ inua kidole cha shahada cha mkono wa kulia, na ukishushe kwa ‘illallah’.",
        "These steps follow the Hanafi method. In the Shafi‘i school: the hands are folded above the navel; the opening dua is ‘Wajjahtu wajhiya…’; Bismillah is recited as part of al-Fatihah and Ameen is said aloud in the loud prayers; the hands are raised when going into ruku‘ and when rising from it; the follower also recites al-Fatihah; and Qunut is read in Fajr after the ruku‘ of the second rak‘ah. Learn the details from a teacher of your school." to "Hatua hizi zinafuata njia ya Hanafi. Katika shule ya Shafi’i: mikono imekunjwa juu ya kitovu; dua ya ufunguzi ni ‘Wajjahtu wajhiya…’; Bismillah inasomwa kama sehemu ya al-Fatihah na Ameen inasemwa kwa sauti kubwa katika sala za sauti; mikono huinuliwa wakati wa kuingia katika rukuu na wakati wa kuinuka kutoka humo; mfuasi pia anasoma al-Fatihah; na Qunut inasomwa Alfajiri baada ya rukuu ya rakaa ya pili. Jifunze maelezo kutoka kwa mwalimu wa shule yako.",
        "These steps follow the Hanafi method. In the Maliki school: the arms are commonly left at the sides; no opening dua, Ta‘awwuz or Bismillah is recited in a Fard prayer; the follower does not recite behind the imam in the loud prayers; Qunut is read quietly in Fajr; and the prayer is ended with one obligatory salam. Learn the details from a teacher of your school." to "Hatua hizi zinafuata njia ya Hanafi. Katika shule ya Maliki: mikono kawaida huachwa kando; hakuna dua ya ufunguzi, Ta‘awwuz au Bismillah inasomwa katika sala ya Fard; mfuasi hasomi nyuma ya imamu katika sala za sauti; Qunut inasomwa kwa utulivu katika Fajr; na swala inamalizikia kwa salamu moja ya faradhi. Jifunze maelezo kutoka kwa mwalimu wa shule yako.",
        "These steps follow the Hanafi method. In the Hanbali school: the same Thana is recited; Ameen is said aloud in the loud prayers; the hands are raised when going into ruku‘ and when rising from it; ‘Rabbighfir li’ between the two sajdahs is required; and Witr is commonly prayed as two rak‘at and then one, with Qunut after ruku‘. Learn the details from a teacher of your school." to "Hatua hizi zinafuata njia ya Hanafi. Katika shule ya Hanbali: Thana hiyo hiyo inasomwa; Ameen husemwa kwa sauti kubwa katika sala za sauti; mikono huinuliwa wakati wa kuingia katika rukuu na wakati wa kuinuka kutoka humo; ‘Rabbighfir li’ kati ya sajdah mbili inahitajika; na Witr inasaliwa kama rakaa mbili na kisha moja, na Qunut baada ya rukuu. Jifunze maelezo kutoka kwa mwalimu wa shule yako.",
        "Before you begin" to "Kabla ya kuanza",
        "Be in wudu with a clean body, clean clothes and a clean place; cover the awrah; make sure the time of the prayer has entered; and stand facing the Qibla." to "Kuwa katika wudhu na mwili safi, nguo safi na mahali safi; funika awrah; hakikisha muda wa maombi umeingia; na simama ukielekea Qibla.",
        "Keep about four fingers' space between the feet." to "Weka nafasi ya vidole vinne kati ya miguu.",
        "Niyyah (intention)" to "Niyyah (nia)",
        "Intend in your heart which prayer you are offering, for example ‘two rak‘at Fard of Fajr, for Allah’. Saying it with the tongue is recommended, not required." to "Amua moyoni mwako ni sala gani unayoswali, kwa mfano ‘rakat mbili za Fard ya Alfajiri, kwa ajili ya Allah’. Inapendekezwa kusema kwa ulimi, sio lazima.",
        "Also intend that you are following this imam." to "Pia kusudia kuwa unamfuata imamu huyu.",
        "Takbir-e-Tahrimah" to "Takbir-e-Tahrimah",
        "Raise both hands until the thumbs touch the earlobes, palms facing the Qibla, and say Allahu Akbar. Then lower them and place the right hand over the left below the navel." to "Inua mikono yote miwili hadi vidole gumba viguse ncha za masikio, viganja vikitazama Qibla, na sema Allahu Akbar. Kisha uwashushe na uweke mkono wa kulia juu ya kushoto chini ya kitovu.",
        "Raise both hands to the shoulders, keeping them inside the shawl, and say Allahu Akbar. Then place the right palm over the back of the left hand on the chest." to "Inua mikono yote miwili hadi mabegani, ukiiweka ndani ya shela, na sema Allahu Akbar. Kisha weka kiganja cha kulia juu ya nyuma ya mkono wa kushoto kwenye kifua.",
        "While standing, keep your eyes on the place of sajdah." to "Ukiwa umesimama weka macho yako kwenye sehemu ya sajdah.",
